# PROPOSAL — FLAG 1: the whole-bake accumulator threading (ruled 2026-10-25)

Bring-for-ruling. NOTHING in this file is landed. Every hunk below is
old-text → new-text against the tree as it stands at `attn-contract` HEAD
+ landed B (ee1ca99b3 + the two B hunks). Line numbers cite the current
file.

## The ruled design (restated)

ONE accumulator across the expansion in bake order:
- wrapper-submitted decode/primary/batch/CB tickets SEED it (panic-class
  door — those paths have no ladder to shorten);
- the serial prefix-free ladder continues from that seed (its existing
  skip-and-stop door, unchanged semantics, now judged against the seed);
- the prefix ladder checks `total_verdict(accumulated + trips)` per rung
  BEFORE submit, skip-and-name, refusal surfacing through
  `prefix_ladder_bakes_every_rung` (loudly, budget named);
- wrapper decode doors STAY panic-class;
- census reports the WHOLE-bake total as one number.

## Bake order of the five wrapper/deferred sites (the thread's spine)

1. `:12957` decode bundle (m=1) — wrapper, seeds.
2. `:13069` decode batch rungs (BATCH_RUNGS, widest first) — wrapper, seeds.
   (`:13002` decode cap buckets are `!sendnn_superdsc` — never coexist.)
3. `:13312` serial prefix-free prefill ladder — existing checked door,
   continues from the seed.
4. `:13484` prefix ladder — SWITCHES from the wrapper to checked deferred
   (this is the fix: it previously submitted through the wrapper's
   immediate submit and never reached `accumulated` at all).
5. `:13616` CB decode bake — wrapper, seeds. Sits AFTER the census write,
   so the census moves below it (hunk 5).

