## Open points for ruling (defaults chosen, yours to overturn)

1. **Batch rungs** (`:13069`) seed through the wrapper → a TOTAL refusal
   there panics, per "wrapper decode doors STAY panic-class". They DO have
   a ladder (a batch can run a narrower rung, in more forwards), so
   skip-and-name could apply — default is the ruling as given: panic.
2. **Census placement** — moved below the CB bake so the number is whole.
   Confirm.
3. **Prefix refusal: continue** (every asked rung attempted and named)
   rather than break. Confirm.
4. **Census content** — `refused_prefix` lines are NOT added to the census
   (not ruled). The every-rung guard panics loudly on any prefix refusal,
   so a green build cannot carry one silently. Say the word if you want
   them recorded anyway.
5. **Wrapper panic text** — "WHOLE-BAKE TOTAL REFUSED — … (the
   decode/primary bake has no ladder to shorten)". Confirm wording.

## Behavior delta

No green build changes until the ceiling is hit: the threading only puts
the decode/batch/CB seed ON TOP of the total the serial ladder already
judged. Run-47's m=31 stop moves EARLIER by the seed; under B ({256,512})
the serial ladder's own projection (~89k at 2× body cut) plus the seed is
what your re-fire measures. The re-fire stays EXPECTED RED by the
per-bundle wall (512 body > 65,536) regardless of this diff — the wall
refuses the rung before any total is consulted.
